This companion page is a dependency leaf. Its examples use the theory on [[affine-coxeter-diagrams-and-semidefinite-classification]] and that page’s established prerequisite closure; no other theory page depends on examples homed here.

The examples make the affine-form criteria concrete: they calculate radicals and slices for small affine diagrams, distinguish the infinity-edge case from finite dihedral groups, compare the B-tilde and C-tilde families, and treat reducible semidefinite forms factorwise. A final example exhibits an indefinite Coxeter form that is not affine. Each item states its hypotheses and verifies its calculations locally.
